the free stack -- _asan_wrap / gyFree / operator delete, all of it in our own
files -- and the use site is entirely third-party, a system DLL reading the
byte.  The ONLY difference between this log and the third-party one is the
frame that sits immediately behind the plumbing: geeyoou::Label::setText here,
SogouPY.ime there.

That one frame is the whole verdict.  If a change to the plumbing skip ever
makes these two agree, one of them is wrong and the classifier is worthless in
one direction or the other.

Also the case a "BOTH sites must be ours" rule would ship: we freed it, they
read it.  One blame stack is enough.
